From cf76881ebac85cad8652fe5fe26f11f311a21e66 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:15:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-8 remaining seven data planes

Add the remaining seven batch-8 Units on top of the reconciled canonical chain.
Base in the reconciled canonical order is the 28-layer chain through 0147
(canonical 75f1d24 plus 0120-0129, 0131, 0134, 0136, 0130, 0133, 0135, 0132,
0137, 0138, 0139, 0140, 0141, 0142, 0143, 0144, 0145, 0146 and 0147); this is
the 29th layer after 0120 and it applies at the chain end.

- oled (U119), mini-oled (U166) and glass2 (U158-B) share a new OLED display
  command-slave kind: SH1107 128x64, SSD1315 72x40 and SSD1309 128x64 command /
  data stream recording with 0x00/0x40 2-wire control bytes, column/page
  addressing, a monochrome framebuffer, contrast/display-on/inverse/start-line
  fixtures, command/data/pixel counters, framebuffer CRC and last-command hex.
  The product page addresses and the frozen driver defaults disagree
  (oled/mini-oled page 0x3C vs driver 0x3D, glass2 page self-contradiction), so
  the driver address is modeled and the page address stays an explicit gap.
  The three display Units conflict on 0x3C/0x3D and the M5Unified external
  display composition / panel optics are NOT modeled.
- nbiot-cn (U112, SIM7020C), lora-e220-920 (U170, E220-900T22S JP/LLCC68) and
  lorawan-us915 (U184-US915, STM32WLE5/RAK3172) use the shared UART TX capture
  and idle-gap fixture responder. lora-e220-920 reuses the 0xC0/C1 config-frame
  echo and exposes config-hex; the 920MHz register bits/RF/certification are
  NOT run and the batch5 433 evidence is not transferable. SIM7020C AT
  firmware/URC/attach ordering and the LoRaWAN US915 product-vs-ASR650x driver
  mismatch remain unresolved; only byte/fixture layers are modeled.
- mic (U096): public UIFlow2 has NO Unit MIC driver (explicit driver gap), so
  the model provides a white-pin SAR-ADC analog-mv fixture and a yellow-pin
  LM393 comparator digital input (comparator-level/digital-level) with an
  adc-samples counter. Acoustic response/threshold/SNR are NOT modeled.

Offline QOM smoke (S3 board, no guest) validates property registration,
fixtures, range rejection and responder defaults; it is not a functional PASS.
